# Findings verified by hand and deliberately silenced, by FINGERPRINT.
#
# Fingerprints pin the exact commit, file and line, so these two entries
# suppress these two findings and nothing else: a real key added to the same
# file tomorrow still fires. A path or regex allowlist would have covered that
# case too, silently, which is the opposite of what a secret scan is for.
#
# Both are in init_wizard.rs, and both are the same joke: the code that FINDS
# ssh keys is flagged for containing the words that identify an ssh key.
#
#   src/cli/init_wizard.rs:611   the discovery branch itself,
#                                `preview.contains("-----BEGIN OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----")`,
#                                which classifies the key files found in ~/.ssh/.
#
#   src/cli/init_wizard.rs:1100  a test fixture. Its body is `b3BlbnNzaC1rZXk=`,
#                                base64 for the twelve bytes "openssh-key".
#
# Checked on 2026-09-10 with gitleaks 8.30.1 against all 302 commits: these are
# the only two findings in the history. The real PVE token that reached this
# repository in an earlier revision (rotated and revoked when discovered, see
# the comment on the secret-scan job in ci.yml) is no longer detected.
